{"id":"chatcmpl-d176f795-afeb-4985-995d-e255a4f7c63b","object":"chat.completion","created":1795248643,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-model consensus strategy for medical image interpretation where conflicting outputs are resolved through a verification step rather than naive aggregation. The key insight is that disagreement between specialized models is a signal to invoke an explicit conflict-resolution mechanism before committing to an answer. The pattern generalizes to any visual QA task where laterality, presence/absence, or fine-grained localization must be determined from ambiguous imaging.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When multiple independent models disagree on a binary or categorical finding, treat the disagreement as a trigger for an explicit verification step rather than defaulting to majority vote or first-model output.\",\n    \"For laterality or localization questions, prompt each model to describe trajectory and position (not just presence) so that reasoning is auditable and conflicts are diagnosable.\",\n    \"Use a dedicated verifier/arbiter tool as a distinct pipeline stage when model outputs conflict, and record the conflict rationale in the verification call.\",\n    \"Prefer specialized domain models for initial detection and a separate cross-validation model for confirmation, rather than relying on a single model's confidence.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"medical_imaging_QA\": \"Route detection and laterality questions through at least two models; when they disagree, escalate to a verifier with the conflict explicitly stated before answering.\",\n    \"multi_model_consensus\": \"Design pipelines with an explicit arbitration stage; capture each model's reasoning (location, trajectory) so conflicts can be resolved on evidence rather than vote counts.\",\n    \"ambiguous_finding_resolution\": \"When a finding's presence is uncertain, ask models to describe supporting visual features; use those descriptions to adjudicate rather than re-asking the same question.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm whether model outputs agree; if not, invoke a verifier with the specific conflict described before finalizing.\",\n    \"Ensure the final answer's laterality/presence claim is backed by at least one model's explicit positional reasoning, not just a label.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":522,"total_tokens":940,"completion_tokens":418,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":522},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":418}}}